<title>FRANCE: EU grants free market grain, none from interventio.</title>
<headline>EU grants free market grain, none from interventio.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following rebates to export free-market grain to non-EU countries, member-country officials said.</p>
<p>			 Tonnage		Maximum rebate</p>
<p> Soft wheat	   71,900		14.50 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Barley		 75,000		27.93 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Rye		     5,000		31.05 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Oats		   33,000		34.90 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>(Finland/Sweden) to non-EU (except Switzerland-Liechstenstein)</p>
<p> Oats		    1,500		32.95 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>(Finland/Sweden to Switzerland/Liechtenstein)</p>
<p>It sold no intervention grain at Thursday's weekly tender, member country officials added.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
